--- ENV-10, ENV-11: the exists predicate ---
a boolean called 'the first reading' is false.
If the environment variable "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_916882" exists then, Set 'the first reading' to true. Print 'the first reading'.
If the environment variable "VOXFUZZ_UNSET_916882" exists then, Print "missing". Otherwise, Print "yes". Print 'the first reading'.
If 'the first reading' then, Print "ASSERT ENV-10: expected 0 got 1", Exit 95. Print 'the first reading'.

    a boolean called 'the street sign' is false,
    If the environment variable "DISPLAY" exists then, Set 'the street sign' to true. Print 'the street sign',
    If the environment variable "DISPLAY" exists then, Print "at home". Otherwise, Print "away". Print 'the street sign',
    Print 'the street sign'.

a boolean called 'the label' is false.
If the environment variable "TERM" exists then, Set 'the label' to true. Print 'the label'.
If the environment variable "TERM" exists then, Print "present". Otherwise, Print "here". Print 'the label'.
Print 'the label'.

--- ENV-03, ENV-04: an entry contains an equals sign ---
a text called 'the street sign' is environment's first.
a buffer called 'the street sign in bytes' is 'the street sign'.
a number called 'the street sign equals signs' is 0.
For each slot from 1 to 'the street sign in bytes''s size, If byte slot of 'the street sign in bytes' is 61 then, Set 'the street sign equals signs' to 'the street sign equals signs' add 1..
If 'the street sign in bytes''s size is not 0 and 'the street sign equals signs' is 0 then, Print "ASSERT ENV-03: expected 1 got {'the street sign equals signs'}", Exit 95. Print 'the street sign equals signs' as a boolean.
Print 'the street sign in bytes''s size as a boolean.

